Revision history for App-Syslogd

0.02	Thu Oct  1 2026
	First CPAN release, as App::Syslogd (the backend of
	https://github.com/nigelhorne/syslogd).
	- Logic moved out of etc/syslogd into App::Syslogd, which
	  etc/syslogd now wraps
	- SIGHUP closes and reopens the log file, for logrotate;
	  SIGTERM/SIGINT stop cleanly
	- Security: the log file is opened with O_NOFOLLOW and mode 0600;
	  symlinks, hard links and files owned by other users are refused
	- Proper CSV via Text::CSV; control characters (including
	  newlines) written as \xNN so each record is one line
	- A message without a valid PRI (0-191) is recorded as user.notice,
	  as RFC 3164 4.3.3 requires, rather than as a hex dump
	- Host names via getnameinfo (honours /etc/hosts), cached with CHI;
	  --no-resolve to log addresses; IPv6 and --address supported
	- Datagrams up to 65535 bytes accepted without truncation
	- Messages localisable through Locale::Maketext (English shipped)
	- new(): an option given as undef now means "use the default"
	  instead of replacing the default with undef
	- process() with an undef sender records the message with an empty
	  Host column instead of dying inside Socket::getnameinfo
	- Windows: no longer dies because Fcntl does not define O_NOFOLLOW
	  there, or because Perl has no fchmod there (an existing log's
	  permissions are left alone); the tests skip what Windows cannot do (permission bits,
	  symlinks, signals) and the real-UDP test no longer relies on
	  alarm() interrupting recv()
	- run() no longer leaves the object marked as running when it dies
	  (e.g. a failed reopen after SIGHUP)
	- t/function.t: white-box tests of every function
	- Documentation rewritten in plain English, with ENCODING, COMMON
	  PITFALLS, FORMAL SPECIFICATION and STATE DIAGRAM sections
